This file contains mandatory instructions for AI coding agents, AI Studio, automated coding systems, and human developers making changes to this repository.

The rules below protect the existing Rentmaikar architecture from accidental simplification, deletion, replacement, or architectural drift.

---

1. PRIMARY RULE

DO NOT redesign, simplify, remove, replace, consolidate, or disable an existing integration, provider, communication channel, routing mechanism, adapter, bridge, webhook, callback, authentication mechanism, payment path, IoT/tracking path, or deployment path merely because another implementation appears to perform the same function.

The existence of apparently duplicated functionality is not sufficient evidence that an integration is redundant.

Before removing or replacing anything:

1. Inspect the current implementation.
2. Inspect its callers.
3. Inspect its adapters/interceptors.
4. Inspect its backend routes.
5. Inspect its webhooks and callbacks.
6. Inspect environment configuration.
7. Inspect regional/capability routing.
8. Inspect fallback/failover relationships.
9. Inspect database dependencies.
10. Inspect CI/CD and deployment dependencies.
11. Check the authoritative architecture documents.
12. Obtain explicit authorization before destructive architectural changes.

Preserve first. Change second. Remove last.

