6. CRITICAL SUPABASE RULE

Whenever this pattern is encountered:

supabase.functions.invoke(...)

DO NOT automatically classify it as a direct frontend Supabase dependency.

First determine whether the call is handled by:

- a catch-all interceptor
- an adapter
- a backend bridge
- a local gateway
- a routing layer
- an HTTP proxy
- an edge-function adapter
- a backend function registry
- another abstraction layer

The required investigation order is:

supabase.functions.invoke(...)
        ↓
Is there an interceptor?
        ↓
Is there an adapter?
        ↓
Is there a backend bridge?
        ↓
Is there a local gateway?
        ↓
Is there a routing layer?
        ↓
What production endpoint actually receives the request?

Only after this investigation may the call be classified as direct or indirect.

Mandatory rule

«Every "supabase.functions.invoke(...)" encountered during an audit or refactor MUST first be checked against the catch-all interceptor/adapter architecture.»

Do not replace or remove the call merely because the literal string "supabase.functions.invoke" appears in frontend code.

